      "query": "RAG",
      "items": [
        {
          "path": "AGENTS.md",
          "title": "AGENTS",
          "reason": "bundle",
          "text": "---\ntitle: \"AGENTS\"\ntype: meta\nlang: en\nrole: schema\nlayer: wiki\ntags:\n  - AI/Wiki\nsummary: |\n  Example schema for retrieval and maintenance in the minimal vault.\n---\n\n# Example Vault Schema\n\nThis schema defines how the LLM should operate on the vault.\n\n## Retrieval\n\nAlways read:\n\n1. `wiki/INDEX.md`\n2. relevant `wiki/concepts/*.md`\n3. raw sources only for verification\n\n## Maintenance\n\n- Keep raw sources immutable\n- Update concept pages before creating duplicates\n- Add wikilinks to canonical pages\n- Update `wiki/INDEX.md` when a durable page is added\n- Run lint after meaningful edits\n",
          "tokenEstimate": 148
        },
        {
          "path": "wiki/INDEX.md",
          "title": "INDEX",
          "reason": "bundle",
          "text": "---\ntitle: \"INDEX\"\ntype: meta\nlang: en\nrole: index\nlayer: wiki\ntags:\n  - AI/Wiki\nsummary: |\n  Entry point for the example vault.\n---\n\n# INDEX\n\n- [[RAG and Knowledge Augmentation]]: retrieval, chunking, and graph-based knowledge support\n- [[Vector Store]]: canonical storage primitive used by many RAG systems\n- [[Chunking]]: segmentation policy that shapes retrieval quality\n- [[LOG]]: maintenance history for durable wiki updates\n",
          "tokenEstimate": 108
        },
        {
          "path": "wiki/concepts/RAG and Knowledge Augmentation.md",
          "title": "RAG and Knowledge Augmentation",
          "reason": "title_match",
          "text": "---\ntitle: \"RAG and Knowledge Augmentation\"\ntype: concept\nlang: en\nrole: concept\nlayer: wiki\ntags:\n  - AI/LLM/RAG\n  - AI/LLM/RAG/Retrieval\nsummary: |\n  RAG combines retrieval with generation and benefits from strong chunking, indexing, and evidence handling.\naliases:\n  - \"RAG\"\n  - \"retrieval augmented generation\"\n---\n\n# RAG and Knowledge Augmentation\n\nSee [[INDEX]], [[Vector Store]], and [[Chunking]].\n\nRAG is not just retrieval. It is a structured evidence path from raw sources into answer synthesis.\n\nIn this minimal vault, [[Chunking]] defines segment quality, [[Vector Store]] anchors retrieval infrastructure, and `raw/example-source.md` remains the underlying evidence layer.\n",
          "tokenEstimate": 172
        },
        {
          "path": "wiki/entities/Chunking.md",
          "title": "Chunking",
          "reason": "backlink",
          "text": "---\ntitle: \"Chunking\"\ntype: entity\nlang: en\nrole: entity\nlayer: wiki\ntags:\n  - AI/LLM/RAG\n  - AI/LLM/RAG/Chunking\nsummary: |\n  Chunking defines how source material is segmented before indexing and strongly affects retrieval quality.\n---\n\n# Chunking\n\nSee [[INDEX]] and [[RAG and Knowledge Augmentation]].\n\nChunking controls segment boundaries before documents enter a [[Vector Store]]. Weak chunking increases retrieval noise and lowers answer quality.\n",
          "tokenEstimate": 113
        },
        {
          "path": "wiki/entities/Vector Store.md",
          "title": "Vector Store",
          "reason": "backlink",
          "text": "---\ntitle: \"Vector Store\"\ntype: entity\nlang: en\nrole: entity\nlayer: wiki\ntags:\n  - AI/LLM/RAG\n  - AI/LLM/RAG/Vector-Stores\nsummary: |\n  Vector stores persist embeddings for similarity search and are common building blocks in RAG systems.\naliases:\n  - \"Vector Database\"\n---\n\n# Vector Store\n\nSee [[INDEX]] and [[RAG and Knowledge Augmentation]].\n\nA vector store is a persistence layer for embeddings. It is useful when [[Chunking]] and retrieval pipelines need fast nearest-neighbor lookup over document segments.\n",
          "tokenEstimate": 128
        },
        {
          "path": "raw/example-source.md",
          "title": "Example Source",
          "reason": "backlink",
          "text": "---\ntitle: \"Example Source\"\ntype: raw_source\nlang: en\nrole: raw_source\nlayer: source\ntags: []\nsummary: |\n  Minimal raw source used for CLI smoke checks.\n---\n\n# Example Source\n\nThis source explains retrieval augmented generation and chunking trade-offs.\n",
          "tokenEstimate": 64
        }
      ],
